    "body": "### Describe the issue\r\n\r\nPlan gives the following error for new installs as of December 30th 2019.\r\n```\r\n[ERROR]: [Plan] Plan Requires internet access on first run to download GeoLite2 Geolocation database.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis causes the geolocation of the plugin to not function.\r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\nMaxMind have changed their distribution model on a very short notice by [posting a blog post on December 18](https://blog.maxmind.com/2019/12/18/significant-changes-to-accessing-and-using-geolite2-databases/) - stating the change is due to having to comply with The California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA)\r\n\r\nThe changes mentioned in the blog post include disabling public distribution of the GeoIP2 database and change of license.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nAn account must be created to get a distribution key for the database. (By the developer)\r\n\r\nTo solve the issue on client side, MaxMind eula acceptance policy setting needs to be introduced. - The EULA can be found here: https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/eula\r\n\r\nTo comply with the eula, the GeoIP database needs to be updated on a regular basis (point 3 under Additional Restrictions).\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nUnfortunately this will take a while to fix, sorry for any inconvenience. Temporary solution is to obtain a copy of GeoIP2 database from MaxMind and placing `GeoIP.dat` in the Plan plugin folder.",
